msgid "Quantum machine learning"
msgstr "Quantum machine learning"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum machine learning {#quantum-machine-learning}"
msgstr "Quantum machine learning {#quantum-machine-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum machine learning (QML) is an emerging field that combines quantum computing and machine learning to explore new ways of analyzing data, \n"
"recognizing patterns, and solving complex computational problems. It applies concepts from quantum mechanics to develop quantum algorithms and machine\n"
"learning models that can run on quantum computers or integrate quantum and classical computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang quantum machine learning (QML) ay isang umuusbong na larangan na pinagsasama ang quantum computing at machine learning para tuklasin ang mga bagong paraan ng pag-analisa ng data, \n"
"pagkilala ng mga pattern, at paglutas ng mga kumplikadong computational na problema. Naglalapat ito ng mga konsepto mula sa quantum mechanics para bumuo ng mga quantum algorithm at mga machine\n"
"learning model na maaaring tumakbo sa mga quantum computer o pagsamahin ang quantum at classical na computing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Research in QML includes quantum neural networks, quantum kernel methods, and hybrid quantum-classical algorithms, which use classical computers to \n"
"optimize models while quantum processors perform specific computations. Although QML might offer advantages for certain tasks, practical benefits over \n"
"classical machine learning remain an active area of research.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasama sa pananaliksik sa QML ang mga quantum neural network, quantum kernel method, at hybrid na quantum-classical na algorithm, na gumagamit ng mga classical na computer para \n"
"i-optimize ang mga model habang ang mga quantum processor ang gumagawa ng mga partikular na computation. Bagaman maaaring may maibigay na bentahe ang QML sa ilang gawain, nananatiling aktibong larangan ng pananaliksik ang mga praktikal na benepisyo nito kumpara sa \n"
"classical na machine learning.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common workflow trains a model mostly on classical hardware, and then uses a quantum processor for a targeted subroutine, such as optimizing the diversity of an ensemble of learners or evaluating a quantum kernel, where quantum effects might provide an advantage over a purely classical approach. With this hybrid structure, you can apply quantum resources to the part of the problem where they can have the most effect, while keeping most of a machine learning pipeline, such as data preprocessing and large-scale training, on classical infrastructure. The application functions on this page follow this pattern: one for classification tasks, and one for feature extraction.\n"
msgstr "Ang karaniwang workflow ay nagsasanay ng model higit sa lahat sa classical na hardware, at pagkatapos ay gumagamit ng quantum processor para sa isang tinarget na subroutine, tulad ng pag-optimize sa diversity ng isang ensemble ng mga learner o pag-evaluate ng quantum kernel, kung saan maaaring magbigay ng bentahe ang mga quantum effect kumpara sa purong classical na pamamaraan. Sa hybrid na istrukturang ito, maaari mong ilapat ang mga quantum resource sa bahagi ng problema kung saan pinakamalaki ang epekto nito, habang pinananatili sa classical na imprastraktura ang karamihan ng machine learning pipeline, tulad ng data preprocessing at malakihang pagsasanay. Sinusunod ng mga application function sa pahinang ito ang pattern na ito: isa para sa mga gawain sa classification, at isa para sa feature extraction.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"application-functions\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Application functions for quantum machine learning {#application-functions-for-quantum-machine-learning}"
msgstr "Mga application function para sa quantum machine learning {#application-functions-for-quantum-machine-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following quantum functions apply this hybrid approach to machine learning tasks, and use quantum hardware at different points of a pipeline:\n"
msgstr "Inilalapat ng mga sumusunod na quantum function ang hybrid na pamamaraang ito sa mga gawain sa machine learning, at gumagamit ng quantum hardware sa iba't ibang punto ng isang pipeline:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Singularity Machine Learning - Classification** solves binary classification problems. You provide your own training data, and the function classically trains an ensemble of learners, then uses a quantum algorithm to optimize that ensemble for diversity and generalization, before returning predictions on new data.\n"
msgstr "Ang **Singularity Machine Learning - Classification** ay lumulutas ng mga binary classification na problema. Ibinibigay mo ang sarili mong training data, at ang function ay nagsasanay nang classical ng ensemble ng mga learner, pagkatapos ay gumagamit ng quantum algorithm para i-optimize ang ensemble na iyon para sa diversity at generalization, bago magbalik ng mga prediction sa bagong data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Rimay Quantum Feature Extraction** adds a preprocessing step to an existing machine learning pipeline. You provide classical tabular data, and the function returns quantum-transformed features generated on quantum hardware. You can use these features on their own, or combine them with your original features, to train a classical model of your choice.\n"
msgstr "Ang **Rimay Quantum Feature Extraction** ay nagdaragdag ng hakbang sa preprocessing sa umiiral na machine learning pipeline. Ibinibigay mo ang classical na tabular data, at ibinabalik ng function ang mga quantum-transformed na feature na nabuo sa quantum hardware. Magagamit mo ang mga feature na ito nang mag-isa, o pagsamahin sa orihinal mong mga feature, para magsanay ng classical na model na gusto mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"IBM Quantum&reg; Functions are a beta feature available only to IBM Quantum Premium Plan, Flex Plan, and On-Prem (through the IBM Quantum Platform API) Plan users. Refer to [Set up IBM Quantum Functions](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions) for instructions on getting access.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga paalala\">\n"
"Ang IBM Quantum&reg; Functions ay isang beta feature na available lamang sa mga gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Premium Plan, Flex Plan, at On-Prem (sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Platform API) Plan. Tingnan ang [Set up IBM Quantum Functions](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions) para sa mga tagubilin kung paano magkaroon ng access.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

